Bug 2016999 - Honor the user-selected calendar when accepting an invitation whose event already exists in another subscribed calendar. r=darktrojan

When accepting an iMIP invitation, the accept operation was bound to whichever subscribed calendar already held the event's UID, so the response was written there and the user's choice in the calendar chooser was ignored. The chooser also preselected the default calendar rather than the one holding the event.

The accept now writes to the calendar the user selected: it updates the event in place when that calendar already has it, otherwise adds a copy there. This also applies when the target calendar is determined without showing the chooser, e.g. when only one calendar matches the invited attendee. The chooser preselects the calendar that holds the event, or the current default calendar when it is not found. The default is read from the `calendar-main-default` property instead of the opening window's composite, whose cached default misses later changes to the selected calendar. The invitation lookup prefers the default calendar first and then the calendars' visible order, so the preselection is deterministic.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310021

